*.exe
*.test
/cmd/debugtools/*/main
market/bin/
websocket/websocket
websocket/websocket-server

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
pump-tokens-ui/build/
pump-tokens-ui/.env.local

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# OS
.DS_Store

# Never commit private keys / certs (found web3ite.cab.key + cert chain
# checked into the working tree — real TLS private key for a live domain,
# must never enter git history)
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx

# Local editor/IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# Never commit real secrets backed up locally during cleanup
*DO_NOT_COMMIT*

# Internal notes / audit docs and deployment runbook — not meant for a public
# portfolio repo (course notes, internal bug-tracking, real infra topology)
docs/
DEPLOY-devnet.md

# NOTE: market/trade/consumer/dataflow/gateway/websocket's etc/*.yaml (non
# -local) production configs are intentionally tracked, NOT gitignored — the
# Dockerfile COPYs them at build time and Railway builds straight from this
# repo, so hiding them breaks the actual deployment (learned this the hard
# way: it crash-looped every service). The repo is private, and the one
# value they carry (the Railway-internal MySQL password) was already
# explicitly approved to stay in-repo. If this repo is ever made public,
# revisit this — but don't gitignore them again without also fixing how
# Railway gets its config.
